\textbf{Theorem 1.} If $n$ is an odd integer, then $n^{2} + 3n + 4$ is an even integer.
\textbf{Theorem 1.} If $k$ is an even integer, then $k^{3} + 2k + 5$ is an odd integer.
\textbf{Theorem 1.} If $k$ is an odd integer, then $k^{2} + 3k + 9$ is an odd integer.
If <m>n</m> is an even integer, then <m>n^{2} + 8n + 9</m> is an odd integer.
